{"name":"Laundry White","hex":"#f6f7f1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"laundry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A laundering; a washing.","A place or room where laundering is done - including, by extension, other forms of laundering than clothes washing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laundry"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laundry","blocks":[{"text":"Laundry is the washing of clothing and other textiles, and, more broadly, their drying and ironing as well. Laundry has been part of history since humans began to wear clothes, so the methods by which different cultures have dealt with this universal human need are of interest to several branches of scholarship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Italian_hanging_laundry.jpg/330px-Italian_hanging_laundry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laundry","wikidata":"Q852100"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Laundry_1806.PNG/500px-Laundry_1806.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Laundry_1806.PNG/500px-Laundry_1806.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Man and woman washing linen in a brook\", from William Henry Pyne's Microcosm (1806). Unusually, this is depicted as a mixed-sex activity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaundry_1806.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg/500px-Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg/1280px-Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg/500px-Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Laundry is being done by a woman in the river, near Kiou Ka Cham, Laos","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Brogi%2C_Carlo_%281850-